/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the early 20th century, kabaddi moved from rural festivals into organized sport. Maharashtra, India, became a hub for kabaddi competitions, and a standardized set of rules emerged by 1950 with the creation of the All India Kabaddi Federation. Kabaddi became an official sport in the Indian Olympic Games in 1951, fueling its popularity across the country. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [8]
>>
